join detective right
detective: There’s a broken vase upstairs.
detective: I need to know who broke it.
join guard left
guard: All I can say is that I didn’t do it. 
guard (angry): Why are you worried about a vase? Aren’t you solving a murder?
guard (speaking): Whatever.
guard: If it was that big, fancy, golden vase in the upstairs hallway, I’m pretty sure it was intact when the Count gave me a tour of the house.
detective (thinking): Okay.
guard: And then the cook came out to let me know the Count had collapsed just minutes after that.
guard: She stayed with me until Narin and Aslan asked us to come upstairs. 
guard: So I suppose she couldn’t have done it either.
